WEBVTT

00:05.100 --> 00:08.177
<i>Narrator:
Stewie Griffin--
scientist, inventor, infant.</i>

00:08.259 --> 00:10.735
<i>Searching for a way to tap
into the hidden strengths</i>

00:10.769 --> 00:11.805
<i>That all humans have.</i>

00:11.873 --> 00:13.412
<i>Then an accidental overdose</i>

00:13.480 --> 00:15.687
<i>Of gamma radiation
alters his body chemistry.</i>

00:15.755 --> 00:17.393
(thunder rumbles)

00:17.461 --> 00:20.222
<i>And now whenever stewie griffin
grows angry or outraged,</i>

00:20.422 --> 00:22.705
A startling metamorphosis occurs.

00:22.854 --> 00:25.764
Oh, I hurt myself changing a tire!

00:28.676 --> 00:29.646
(thunder rumbles)

00:32.877 --> 00:35.520
<i>NARRATOR:
The creature is driven by rage</i>

00:35.604 --> 00:37.610
<i>and pursued by
an investigative reporter.</i>

00:37.678 --> 00:39.719
Mr. Tucker, don't
make me angry.

00:39.787 --> 00:41.358
You wouldn't like
me when I'm angry.

00:52.502 --> 00:55.679
<i>NARRATOR:
The creature is wanted for
a murder he didn't commit.</i>

00:55.748 --> 00:58.992
<i>Stewie Griffin
is believed to be dead.</i>

00:59.060 --> 01:01.635
<i>And he must let the world
think that he is dead,</i>

01:01.703 --> 01:03.710
<i>until he can find a way
to control</i>

01:03.778 --> 01:06.454
<i>the raging spirit
that dwells within him.</i>

01:06.522 --> 01:07.893
(roars)

01:16.493 --> 01:19.336
Oh, come on, can we please
change the channel?

01:19.404 --> 01:20.675
I can't stand
local news.

01:20.743 --> 01:22.482
No, Brian.
The new female anchor

01:22.550 --> 01:24.657
is about to do that
Child of the Month segment.

01:24.724 --> 01:26.095
I like her.

01:26.164 --> 01:28.102
Good evening,
I'm Joyce Kinney.

01:28.171 --> 01:30.446
<i>And this is April's
Child of the Month,</i>

01:30.514 --> 01:32.687
<i>eight-year-old Angus Reed.</i>

01:32.755 --> 01:34.929
<i>Angus was born
with cerebral palsy.</i>

01:34.998 --> 01:38.242
<i>And his only wish is to one day
become a famous heart surgeon.</i>

01:38.311 --> 01:41.088
All I want to do is help people.

01:41.155 --> 01:43.161
<i>Child of the Month, Angus Reed.</i>

01:43.229 --> 01:44.701
<i>Good luck with
your dream, Angus.</i>

01:44.769 --> 01:45.905
<i>We believe in you.</i>

01:45.973 --> 01:47.344
What a weird little guy.

01:47.412 --> 01:48.615
Thanks, Joyce.

01:48.683 --> 01:50.690
How old do they usually
live to be, by the way?

01:50.759 --> 01:52.498
Well, you never see
a gray-haired one.

01:52.565 --> 01:55.006
Ah, so inspiring.

01:55.075 --> 01:57.951
(church bells ringing)

02:02.437 --> 02:04.075
Mom, there's a row
open up there.

02:04.142 --> 02:06.148
Oh, good, I like
sitting in the front.

02:06.217 --> 02:07.488
Me, too.

02:07.556 --> 02:08.959
<i>I didn't dress up
not to be seen.</i>

02:11.905 --> 02:14.279
Hey, you, go easy on
the communion wine today.

02:14.348 --> 02:16.656
Don't want another one
of your drunken mishaps.

02:16.724 --> 02:18.262
(baby talk):
Let me get at that belly.

02:18.330 --> 02:19.500
Let me kiss that belly.
(laughing)

02:19.567 --> 02:20.537
Stop it!
Cut it out!

02:20.605 --> 02:21.809
I'm gonna give you
a flubber kiss.

02:21.877 --> 02:22.813
Oh, Lois,
that tickles!

02:22.881 --> 02:25.121
Flubber-belly,
pork-belly Stewie.

02:25.189 --> 02:26.996
(blows raspberries)

02:27.063 --> 02:28.367
(both laughing)

02:28.434 --> 02:30.508
Ah, give me that belly!

02:30.577 --> 02:32.617
(blows raspberries)

02:32.668 --> 02:34.523
(groaning)
(coughing)

02:34.592 --> 02:36.901
(screaming)

02:36.969 --> 02:38.039
Oh, my God!

02:38.105 --> 02:40.448
(screaming)

02:40.516 --> 02:41.987
I'm sorry.
(chuckles)

02:42.055 --> 02:44.563
I got a little nervous.

02:44.631 --> 02:47.073
It's just,
I like you so much.

02:47.140 --> 02:49.950
Please turn to hymn number 487.

02:50.018 --> 02:52.996
(organ playing hymn)

02:53.063 --> 02:59.352
♪ If we praise Jesus
by singing all together ♪

02:59.403 --> 03:04.289
♪ It makes this whole exercise
seem less bizarre ♪

03:04.373 --> 03:07.083
♪ Than it really is
when you actually stand back ♪

03:07.151 --> 03:10.227
♪ And examine it
with some objectivity ♪

03:10.295 --> 03:15.281
♪ Amen. ♪

03:15.348 --> 03:17.254
PRIEST:
Please be seated.

03:17.322 --> 03:19.931
Let me remind you all that
this Saturday at 5:00 p.m.,

03:20.000 --> 03:22.140
we'll have vespers,
not to be confused

03:22.208 --> 03:23.813
with the Italian motor scooter.

03:23.881 --> 03:27.727
(polite laughter,
Lois laughing loudly)

03:27.795 --> 03:29.635
(Lois continues laughing)

03:29.703 --> 03:32.144
LOIS:
Vespers!

03:32.212 --> 03:34.152
And don't forget, next weekend,

03:34.220 --> 03:36.394
we will have the Sunday
afternoon family picnic--

03:36.464 --> 03:38.771
as God said to Noah--
weather permitting.

03:38.839 --> 03:41.180
(polite laughter,
Lois laughing loudly)

03:41.247 --> 03:43.623
(Lois continues laughing)

03:43.690 --> 03:45.262
Stop it!

03:45.330 --> 03:47.504
And another reminder:
When you arrive to mass,

03:47.572 --> 03:49.612
please do not park
behind the rectory.

03:49.681 --> 03:53.159
As the Corinthians said to
the Galatians, "That's my land."

03:53.228 --> 03:54.297
(polite laughter,
Lois laughing loudly)

03:54.364 --> 03:55.668
Oh, ho, ho!

03:55.737 --> 03:57.308
Look out, Gallagher!

03:57.376 --> 03:58.547
PETER:
Stop kissing ass.

04:00.388 --> 04:01.324
Bless you.

04:01.391 --> 04:02.327
Have a wonderful day.

04:02.395 --> 04:03.230
Thank you, Father.

04:05.374 --> 04:06.877
Hey, nice talk, chief.

04:06.946 --> 04:08.852
There you go.
Buy the wife something pretty.

04:08.921 --> 04:11.696
Oh, Father, your homily
was so moving today.

04:11.765 --> 04:12.967
Thank you, Lois.

04:13.036 --> 04:14.875
And thank you for
the great job you did

04:14.943 --> 04:16.783
with the rummage sale for
the needy last weekend.

04:16.850 --> 04:18.924
Oh, it was my pleasure.

04:18.992 --> 04:22.438
You know, I accidentally almost
put a cashmere sweater in there.

04:22.505 --> 04:23.943
Can you believe?
(chuckles)

04:24.011 --> 04:26.453
What would one of them do
with a cashmere sweater?

04:26.520 --> 04:29.129
You know, Lois, we also
have a bake sale coming up,

04:29.197 --> 04:30.836
and we're short
about eight pies.

04:30.903 --> 04:32.944
Well, I'll hit the grocery store
this afternoon

04:33.013 --> 04:34.248
and get to work.

04:34.317 --> 04:35.320
PETER:
Okay, Lois, bye!

04:35.388 --> 04:36.424
Bye, church!

04:36.492 --> 04:37.630
Bye, church guy!

04:37.698 --> 04:39.504
Bye, unending conversation!

04:39.570 --> 04:41.009
Bye, terrible church people!

04:41.077 --> 04:42.113
Bye!

04:46.732 --> 04:49.943
My God, does everything have
to have a mascot these days?

04:50.012 --> 04:53.055
I mean, look, there's a lion in
overalls on the aluminum foil.

04:53.123 --> 04:54.862
I mean, wh-who
is that for?

04:54.930 --> 04:56.368
No, Lois, don't
get that one!

04:56.435 --> 04:58.476
Get the one with the
lion in overalls!

04:58.543 --> 05:00.584
(gasps)
Oh, my God, look!

05:00.652 --> 05:03.294
It's Joyce Kinney
from Channel Five.

05:03.362 --> 05:05.503
Excuse me, Miss Kinney?

05:05.570 --> 05:08.915
I don't mean to bother you,
but my name is Lois Griffin.

05:08.983 --> 05:11.491
I-I am a huge fan,
and I just think

05:11.560 --> 05:13.650
you are doing
a fantastic job.

05:13.718 --> 05:16.059
And after what I went through
with Diane Simmons,

05:16.128 --> 05:17.398
well, let me
just say it's nice

05:17.466 --> 05:19.774
to be standing here
with no one trying to murder me.

05:19.841 --> 05:21.514
Yeah, no, you're fine.

05:21.581 --> 05:23.955
Oh, well, that's very
nice of you to say.

05:24.024 --> 05:26.031
You know, it's my
first anchoring job,

05:26.099 --> 05:27.670
and I'm trying to make
a good impression.

05:27.738 --> 05:29.711
I love the "Child
of the Month" segment.

05:29.779 --> 05:31.953
We just watched that one
with the little goofball

05:32.021 --> 05:33.860
who thought he was
going to be a doctor.

05:33.929 --> 05:36.940
Ah, I can't believe
I'm actually meeting you.

05:37.007 --> 05:39.249
You know, the news is so much
better with you on it.

05:39.317 --> 05:40.989
Well, you know, Lois,

05:41.057 --> 05:43.332
I'm on my way back to
the station after lunch.

05:43.398 --> 05:45.004
I'd be happy to
give you a tour.

05:45.073 --> 05:48.619
Oh, my goodness.
That'd be wonderful.

05:48.685 --> 05:50.157
Great. Why don't
you come down

05:50.225 --> 05:51.445
to the station
around 6:00?

05:51.513 --> 05:52.516
You can watch
the broadcast.

05:52.584 --> 05:54.540
Okay. I'll see you then.

05:56.951 --> 05:58.606
Oh, wait-wait.

05:58.673 --> 05:59.961
BILF.
Total BILF.

06:02.053 --> 06:03.190
Yeah, so, going pretty good.

06:03.257 --> 06:06.034
I got six pacifiers now.

06:06.102 --> 06:07.641
That was a big nothing.

06:11.488 --> 06:13.627
And Julie Andrews
pleaded not guilty,

06:13.696 --> 06:14.899
saying that she
brought the gun

06:14.968 --> 06:16.405
to the nightclub
for protection.

06:16.474 --> 06:18.948
And that's all for today's
Channel Five News at 6:00.

06:19.016 --> 06:20.253
Oh, I almost forgot.

06:20.322 --> 06:21.725
That little girl
is still missing.

06:21.794 --> 06:23.382
Do we have a picture?

06:23.450 --> 06:25.624
Do we... We-we don't?
We don't have a picture?

06:25.692 --> 06:27.297
Okay, we don't have
a picture. Okay.

06:27.364 --> 06:28.903
But she's...
She's Puerto Rican.

06:28.971 --> 06:32.049
So look out
for a Puerto Rican.

06:32.117 --> 06:35.629
(news theme playing)

06:35.696 --> 06:38.406
We're clear.

06:38.474 --> 06:40.280
That was so much
fun to watch.

06:40.349 --> 06:41.686
What a pro you are.

06:41.754 --> 06:43.024
Lois,
you've met Tom Tucker.

06:43.092 --> 06:44.631
Oh, yes, of course.

06:44.698 --> 06:46.069
I loved that
piece you did

06:46.138 --> 06:47.542
on the invention
of the guillotine.

06:47.609 --> 06:48.780
Oh, thank you.
You know,

06:48.848 --> 06:50.487
half the time those things
didn't really work.

06:50.555 --> 06:52.126
How was it, honey?

06:52.194 --> 06:53.731
Ah, they couldn't finish.

06:53.800 --> 06:54.937
Oh, really?

06:55.004 --> 06:56.475
Yeah, I got
to go back tomorrow.

06:56.544 --> 06:57.981
Oh, well, I made
cabbage for dinner.

06:58.049 --> 07:01.428
Yeah, that would be
the ending to this day.

07:01.495 --> 07:03.168
In here is our editor, Mike.

07:03.236 --> 07:04.540
They let him smoke inside

07:04.608 --> 07:05.778
because all the smoke
from his cigarette

07:05.845 --> 07:07.684
just floats directly back up
into his face.

07:07.753 --> 07:09.325
(hoarsely): Hey, Joyce,
when you get a chance,

07:09.392 --> 07:11.466
come take a look
at the Weekapaug thing.

07:11.534 --> 07:13.708
Oh, this is all
so fascinating.

07:13.776 --> 07:15.348
You must have
so many stories.

07:15.416 --> 07:18.493
Well, look, if you want to grab
a drink with me later tonight,

07:18.560 --> 07:20.199
I'd be happy to
tell you some.

07:20.267 --> 07:22.174
Oh, my God,
I would love to.

07:22.242 --> 07:23.479
Look at me, huh?

07:23.546 --> 07:25.721
Stepping out on the town
with a big celebrity.

07:25.789 --> 07:27.862
Well, I think
you're exaggerating.

07:27.930 --> 07:31.309
No, you're a lady big shot,
like Miss Piggy.

07:31.377 --> 07:32.780
Hey, Kermit.

07:32.849 --> 07:34.856
What happened to the
"Bears in Space" sketch?

07:34.924 --> 07:36.663
Sorry, it's
"Pigs in Space" now.

07:36.731 --> 07:37.968
There's been a change.

07:38.036 --> 07:39.507
What?
There's been a change!

07:42.855 --> 07:44.259
<i>TV ANNOUNCER:
We now return to</i>

07:44.327 --> 07:46.667
Ellen Only Talks
When Her Guest Is Talking.

07:46.735 --> 07:47.939
So, you want to
hear about my movie?

07:48.007 --> 07:49.311
I had a great weekend.
We spent three

07:49.379 --> 07:50.851
months shooting
in Louisiana.

07:50.919 --> 07:52.357
I danced all over my house.
And, you know, it's a thriller.

07:52.425 --> 07:53.929
It's really a love story, too.
I try to dance in every room

07:53.997 --> 07:55.769
at least once a week. I also
listen to jazz while I vacuum,

07:55.837 --> 07:57.476
which is cool.

07:57.544 --> 07:58.982
Anyway, it comes out
Friday. I got to work

07:59.049 --> 08:00.555
with Julianna Marguiles.
My pets were going wild

08:00.622 --> 08:02.060
all weekend. I think there's,
like, something in the air.

08:02.128 --> 08:03.566
Could not have been nicer.
Like smog or pollen.

08:03.633 --> 08:05.707
Or pollinated smog, or...

08:05.776 --> 08:07.213
Are you just gonna talk

08:07.280 --> 08:09.019
over everything that I say?
I love talking on TV.

08:09.088 --> 08:10.826
I'll-I'll do anything
to talk on TV.

08:10.895 --> 08:12.801
Hiya, lame asses.

08:12.870 --> 08:15.779
(all shouting in protest)

08:15.847 --> 08:17.352
Whoa. We were having
a nice time.

08:17.419 --> 08:19.326
Sorry. I'm just
painfully aware

08:19.394 --> 08:21.066
that I'm the only
member of this family

08:21.134 --> 08:24.379
who's going out for drinks
with a celebrity tonight.

08:24.446 --> 08:25.783
What are you talking about?

08:25.852 --> 08:28.127
Joyce Kinney invited
me out for drinks.

08:28.194 --> 08:29.364
(laughs)

08:29.432 --> 08:31.138
So just order a pizza
or something, okay?

08:31.205 --> 08:32.743
See you guys later.

08:32.811 --> 08:35.053
Man, I hate calling
that pizza place.

08:35.120 --> 08:37.027
They don't speak English, and
they always mess up the order.

08:37.095 --> 08:39.838
It's like trying to give my cell
phone number to the housekeeper.

08:39.906 --> 08:42.549
Okay, I'm expecting a very
important delivery at the house.

08:42.617 --> 08:44.122
So, could you please
call me if it arrives?

08:44.190 --> 08:45.192
I'll give you
my cell number.

08:45.259 --> 08:46.564
Okay. Yes.

08:46.633 --> 08:48.672
No problem.
Give me number.

08:48.740 --> 08:53.457
Okay. 401-555-1125.

08:53.525 --> 08:56.000
Four...

08:57.105 --> 08:59.079
(sighs)
Four, zero...

08:59.147 --> 09:01.923
Four, four, zero...

09:01.990 --> 09:03.362
No, no, I was just
repeating the four.

09:03.430 --> 09:04.566
One four.

09:04.634 --> 09:07.376
One, four...

09:07.445 --> 09:08.448
All right,
let's start over.

09:08.515 --> 09:10.321
Four, zero, one.

09:10.389 --> 09:11.560
Four.

09:11.627 --> 09:12.897
Zero.

09:12.966 --> 09:14.203
Zero...

09:14.271 --> 09:15.240
One.

09:15.308 --> 09:16.344
One.

09:16.412 --> 09:18.519
Four, zero, one.
Yes.

09:18.588 --> 09:20.460
Five, five, five.

09:20.528 --> 09:24.040
Five. Five. Five.

09:24.108 --> 09:25.278
That was painless.

09:25.346 --> 09:28.055
Okay.
One, one, two, five.

09:28.123 --> 09:30.866
One one, two five.

09:30.934 --> 09:32.272
There you go, you got it.

09:32.339 --> 09:33.644
One, five, five.

09:33.711 --> 09:34.915
What?

09:34.982 --> 09:38.195
You say, "One one,
two fives."

09:38.262 --> 09:40.236
One, five, five.

09:40.304 --> 09:42.043
No, no. Not one one
and two fives.

09:42.110 --> 09:43.348
Two ones.

09:43.417 --> 09:47.363
Two, one, one,
one, two, five.

09:47.431 --> 09:48.568
Oh, my God.

09:48.636 --> 09:50.543
Okay. How many ones?

09:50.611 --> 09:52.383
I'm not giving you
quantities of the numbers,

09:52.451 --> 09:53.621
I'm giving you the numbers.

09:53.688 --> 09:54.826
One, one, two, five.

09:54.894 --> 09:56.163
Those are the
last four numbers.

09:56.231 --> 09:58.607
Okay, one...

09:58.675 --> 10:00.213
One, one.

10:00.281 --> 10:02.488
One, one.

10:02.555 --> 10:03.927
Two.
Two.

10:03.995 --> 10:05.131
Five.

10:05.199 --> 10:07.039
Five. Oh, I see.

10:07.106 --> 10:08.879
One, one, two, five.

10:08.947 --> 10:10.652
Yes! One, one, two, five.

10:10.720 --> 10:11.857
All right, now,
read the number back to me.

10:11.925 --> 10:14.734
L-Let me get my pen.

10:18.483 --> 10:21.293
And that's why whenever
I have sex without protection,

10:21.361 --> 10:23.502
I call it, "taking
a John Chancellor."

10:23.569 --> 10:25.777
(both laughing)

10:25.845 --> 10:29.592
Oh, my God, Joyce, you've
got so many great stories.

10:29.659 --> 10:31.332
Oh, come on,
I'm sure

10:31.400 --> 10:33.372
you've done some
crazy stuff in your time.

10:33.440 --> 10:34.744
Well...

10:34.812 --> 10:36.418
Oh, what is it?

10:36.485 --> 10:37.956
No, n-n-no, I can't.

10:38.024 --> 10:40.902
Lois, I feel like we're
really bonding here tonight.

10:40.970 --> 10:42.240
Come on, let's hear it.

10:42.308 --> 10:46.423
Well, I have had an abortion.

10:46.491 --> 10:47.962
(snoring)

10:48.030 --> 10:49.602
Oh, wake me up
when you got something good.

10:49.670 --> 10:52.546
Oh, my goodness,
sarcastic sleeping.

10:52.614 --> 10:54.320
That puts a lot
of pressure on me.

10:54.387 --> 10:57.867
All right, well,
when I was in college,

10:57.934 --> 11:00.409
I was in an adult film.

11:00.477 --> 11:02.919
Oh, my God,
you did a porno?

11:02.987 --> 11:06.031
Shh! Please, please, please
do not say a word to anybody.

11:06.099 --> 11:08.807
I have never told anyone
that, not even my husband.

11:08.876 --> 11:10.749
I promise,
I'll take it to the grave,

11:10.816 --> 11:14.029
But oh, my God, Lois,
that's hilarious!

11:14.095 --> 11:15.501
Do you have a copy?

11:15.569 --> 11:17.341
Oh, no, that movie's
long gone.

11:17.409 --> 11:19.315
<i>Like the original
ending to Grease.</i>

11:19.367 --> 11:21.674
<i>♪ ...together ♪
♪ Rama-lama, ding-dong ♪</i>

11:21.758 --> 11:24.334
<i>♪ We'll always be together ♪
♪ De pom, de pom, de pom,
de pom ♪</i>

11:24.386 --> 11:25.739
<i>♪ Rama-lama ding-dong... ♪</i>

11:25.807 --> 11:28.282
(wind whistling)

11:28.350 --> 11:30.023
We've been up here
for four days.

11:30.090 --> 11:31.895
Why did you drive
the car into the air

11:31.964 --> 11:34.005
if you didn't know how
to get it back down?

11:34.072 --> 11:36.581
Look, Sandy, it seemed like
a good idea at the time.

11:36.649 --> 11:38.236
Obviously,
I didn't think ahead.

11:38.322 --> 11:39.661
It's so cold.

11:39.728 --> 11:41.935
Let's cuddle together
for warmth.

11:42.003 --> 11:44.746
I-I'm... I'm, I'm,
I'm warm enough.

11:47.726 --> 11:49.631
Quick, we gotta
turn the channel.

11:49.700 --> 11:52.375
I promised my friend Joyce
I'd watch the news tonight.

11:52.443 --> 11:55.754
♪ Channel Five ♪

11:55.823 --> 11:59.369
♪ We're there for you ♪

11:59.436 --> 12:02.381
♪ When times are tough ♪

12:02.448 --> 12:05.659
♪ We'll help you through ♪

12:05.727 --> 12:08.938
♪ With news and sports
and weather ♪

12:09.007 --> 12:12.184
♪ We'll always be together ♪

12:12.253 --> 12:15.496
♪ We're with you
through it all ♪

12:15.565 --> 12:18.341
♪ Channel Five. ♪

12:18.409 --> 12:20.282
Holy (beep), that just
turned out awful.

12:20.349 --> 12:21.619
Joyce, do your thing.

12:21.688 --> 12:23.026
Thanks, Tom.

12:23.093 --> 12:25.301
Pornography.
The very word conjures up

12:25.368 --> 12:28.078
images of red-light districts,
unprotected sex, and of course,

12:28.146 --> 12:31.223
the turn-of-the-century
pornograph machine.

12:31.291 --> 12:32.797
(gears clicking)

12:32.865 --> 12:35.004
Whoa-ho-ho! Sweet Mary!

12:37.816 --> 12:40.995
But it seems pornography
has finally found its way

12:41.062 --> 12:42.468
to our neighborhood.

12:42.536 --> 12:46.249
Yes, local housewife and
church organist Lois Griffin

12:46.316 --> 12:47.955
has revealed to this reporter

12:48.024 --> 12:50.030
that she appeared
in a pornographic movie

12:50.097 --> 12:51.702
back in the early 1980s.

12:51.770 --> 12:53.542
What?!
Mom, that's you!

12:53.611 --> 12:55.049
(laughs)

12:55.117 --> 12:58.529
Boy, that black bar would be
a lot lower now, huh? Huh?

12:58.597 --> 13:00.870
Huh? Would it not?

13:00.939 --> 13:04.652
Evidently, Lois Griffin,
star citizen of Quahog,

13:04.720 --> 13:07.329
is also Lois Griffin,
star of "Quest for Fur."

13:07.397 --> 13:09.236
It just goes to show
you never know

13:09.305 --> 13:11.043
what sort of person
is living next door.

13:11.111 --> 13:12.280
Tom?

13:12.349 --> 13:14.390
I can't
believe this!

13:14.457 --> 13:15.827
Lois, you were in a porno?

13:15.896 --> 13:17.802
She totally betrayed me!

13:17.870 --> 13:20.680
I thought girlfriends were
supposed to support each other.

13:20.748 --> 13:23.022
Ha! Slut!

13:30.128 --> 13:32.000
How could you do
that to me, Joyce?!

13:32.068 --> 13:33.975
Oh. Hello, Lois.

13:34.043 --> 13:35.949
I told you that in confidence!

13:36.016 --> 13:37.822
You totally humiliated me!

13:37.890 --> 13:39.730
Well, then I guess
now we're even.

13:39.798 --> 13:40.935
What?!

13:41.004 --> 13:42.408
What are you talking about?

13:42.475 --> 13:44.148
I never did anything to you!

13:44.215 --> 13:46.457
You really don't
remember me, do you?

13:46.525 --> 13:47.694
Remember you?

13:47.762 --> 13:49.601
We went to high
school together, Lois?

13:49.670 --> 13:51.677
Chemistry class?
Freshman year?

13:51.745 --> 13:53.015
Joycie?

13:53.082 --> 13:55.960
You're Joyce
Chevapravatdumrong?

13:56.028 --> 13:58.234
Yes, but they'd never
let that name on TV,

13:58.303 --> 13:59.775
so I changed it to Kinney.

13:59.843 --> 14:02.886
You ruined my adolescence, Lois.

14:02.954 --> 14:05.228
<i>You told me
I'd made the cheer squad,</i>

14:05.295 --> 14:06.902
<i>blindfolded me, and told me</i>

14:06.969 --> 14:09.445
<i>we were going for a special
celebration breakfast.</i>

14:09.513 --> 14:11.452
<i>When you took
the blindfold off,</i>

14:11.520 --> 14:13.460
<i>I was standing
in front of the entire school</i>

14:13.511 --> 14:16.271
<i>with my pants around my ankles
and a hot dog in my mouth.</i>

14:16.338 --> 14:18.144
(laughter)

14:20.621 --> 14:22.795
It was a horrible
thing to do, Lois.

14:22.864 --> 14:25.472
Look, Joyce,
that was a long time ago.

14:25.540 --> 14:27.513
And I'm very sorry
for what I did.

14:27.581 --> 14:29.186
But we're adults now,

14:29.254 --> 14:30.960
and that doesn't
give you any reason

14:31.027 --> 14:32.633
to humiliate me like this.

14:32.700 --> 14:34.238
Boo-hoo.

14:34.307 --> 14:36.748
You don't like it,
you can go talk to a reporter.

14:36.817 --> 14:38.857
Oh, my God.

14:38.924 --> 14:40.463
I thought we
were friends.

14:40.530 --> 14:43.274
The kind of really good friends
that communicate with each other

14:43.341 --> 14:44.880
poorly through Facebook.

14:57.095 --> 14:59.135
Everyone, I think
it's important

14:59.203 --> 15:01.645
that we talk openly
about this.

15:01.713 --> 15:05.041
It was back in a disgusting
period known as the early '80s.

15:05.125 --> 15:07.416
It was a time
when women would stand topless,

15:07.501 --> 15:09.876
high on coke,
on the edge of hotel balconies

15:09.926 --> 15:12.051
while the curtains
were billowing around them.

15:12.119 --> 15:14.526
I think there was actually
more wind back then.

15:14.595 --> 15:15.899
♪ ♪

15:15.967 --> 15:19.010
MAN:
Hey, Lois, get back inside!

15:19.077 --> 15:21.420
This coke isn't
gonna snort itself!

15:21.487 --> 15:23.561
Great party, Raoul.

15:23.629 --> 15:26.104
I feel like I'm horkin'
all your cocaine.

15:26.172 --> 15:27.877
Hey, that's okay, Lois.

15:27.945 --> 15:29.952
You can just buy
the next bag, eh?

15:30.020 --> 15:31.357
Right, other guy?

15:31.425 --> 15:33.198
♪ ♪

15:35.340 --> 15:36.811
Oh, I couldn't
afford that.

15:36.879 --> 15:39.622
My daddy's making me pay for
my own tuition this semester

15:39.691 --> 15:41.865
because I maxed out
all my credit cards

15:41.932 --> 15:44.575
<i>buying a copy of E.T.
at the video store.</i>

15:44.643 --> 15:46.885
It was $399.

15:46.952 --> 15:48.256
Yeah, but you own it.

15:48.324 --> 15:49.996
You can just
watch that now.

15:50.063 --> 15:53.978
And besides, I got another way
you can make money.

15:54.046 --> 15:56.588
So Raoul gave me a job
at his pet store,

15:56.656 --> 15:58.295
but I still
needed money.

15:58.362 --> 16:00.403
One day
I was cleaning a bird cage,

16:00.470 --> 16:04.284
and a porn producer came in,
and... well, the rest you know.

16:04.352 --> 16:07.463
I kind of feel like, the part
that we should have seen was...

16:07.531 --> 16:09.136
You know what?
Never mind. It works.

16:09.204 --> 16:10.340
Good Lord.

16:10.408 --> 16:11.880
Am I a porn baby?

16:11.948 --> 16:13.352
No. Stewie, come on.

16:13.420 --> 16:14.724
I-I doubt it.

16:14.791 --> 16:15.894
I mean, maybe, yeah.

16:15.963 --> 16:17.000
Probably, yes.

16:20.178 --> 16:22.119
(crowd chatter)

16:22.170 --> 16:23.657
Your mom's in a porno!

16:23.709 --> 16:24.896
I saw her boobs!

16:24.964 --> 16:26.101
Shut up!

16:26.169 --> 16:28.007
Hey, Griffin,
your mom's a whore!

16:28.075 --> 16:29.814
Come on, guys,
knock it off!

16:29.883 --> 16:31.889
Yeah, Griffin, your
mom's gross and nasty!

16:31.957 --> 16:33.529
Hey!
Not cool!

16:33.596 --> 16:34.901
That's
a dude's mom!

16:34.969 --> 16:37.076
<i>Well... she's
also my mom.</i>

16:37.143 --> 16:38.381
Aw, your mom's
a whore!

16:38.449 --> 16:39.618
Yeah! Suck it!

16:39.686 --> 16:40.890
You're a
whore-daughter!

16:40.958 --> 16:42.430
Yeah, Griffin
gets it!

16:42.498 --> 16:44.371
(bell tolling)

16:47.450 --> 16:49.457
Boy, I'm really
looking forward to this.

16:49.525 --> 16:52.100
I really need some church
after the week I've had.

16:52.168 --> 16:54.376
(crowd murmuring)

16:58.425 --> 16:59.512
(coughs)
Sinner.

16:59.597 --> 17:00.684
(coughs)
Harlot.

17:00.767 --> 17:01.905
(coughs)
Skank.

17:01.972 --> 17:03.143
(coughing)
I'm actually sick.

17:03.211 --> 17:06.455
You are no longer
welcome here, Lois Griffin.

17:06.523 --> 17:09.165
But, Father, I've been an active
member of this church for...

17:09.234 --> 17:10.905
Leave this house of God!

17:10.974 --> 17:12.344
(crowd chattering)

17:12.412 --> 17:14.921
But-but I love the church.

17:14.988 --> 17:16.995
It's an important part
of my life.

17:17.064 --> 17:19.639
Maybe you should've thought
of that before you made a porn.

17:19.707 --> 17:21.245
But, Father,
I didn't mean...

17:21.312 --> 17:22.784
Wait. Did you
say "a porn?"

17:22.852 --> 17:24.390
Yes.
Oh.

17:24.459 --> 17:26.198
Well, that's kind of weird.
Why?

17:26.266 --> 17:27.669
Well, I mean,
you'd either say,

17:27.738 --> 17:29.677
"You made porn,"
or "You made a porno."

17:29.746 --> 17:31.250
Y-You don't say,
"Made a porn."

17:31.318 --> 17:32.856
It just...
It hits the ear wrong.

17:32.923 --> 17:35.934
Oh, God, have I been saying
it wrong this whole time?

17:39.884 --> 17:41.120
(crying)

17:41.189 --> 17:42.828
Come on, Lois.

17:42.896 --> 17:45.237
If it makes you feel
any better, I don't care.

17:45.305 --> 17:47.814
And what does it matter what
those people in church think?

17:47.881 --> 17:50.507
I mean, most of of them are
just random background people

17:50.575 --> 17:51.745
we've never seen
before anyway.

17:51.814 --> 17:53.151
Half of them
don't even move;

17:53.218 --> 17:54.523
the other
half just blink.

17:54.591 --> 17:56.028
Peter, that-that's
very sweet,

17:56.097 --> 17:58.404
but how am I supposed
to live in this town

17:58.472 --> 17:59.676
if I'm a social pariah?

17:59.744 --> 18:00.981
What's that?

18:01.048 --> 18:02.955
Is that them little
fish that eat cows?

18:03.023 --> 18:04.929
Just-just
leave me alone, please.

18:04.997 --> 18:06.669
(sighs)

18:10.267 --> 18:12.608
Hey, Lois, can I talk
to you for a second?

18:12.676 --> 18:14.115
For the last time, Brian,

18:14.183 --> 18:15.988
there's no link to it
anywhere online.

18:16.056 --> 18:18.397
No, no, that-that's not...
that's not what I'm here for.

18:19.938 --> 18:21.576
Look, Lois, you
did what you did,

18:21.643 --> 18:23.449
and there's nothing you
can change about that.

18:23.518 --> 18:24.789
But those people can only

18:24.857 --> 18:26.761
make you feel ashamed
if you let them.

18:26.830 --> 18:28.703
If you own the
choice that you made,

18:28.770 --> 18:30.142
you-you take away
all their power

18:30.210 --> 18:31.715
to make you feel
bad about yourself.

18:31.782 --> 18:33.019
What do you mean?

18:33.087 --> 18:34.693
Well, you remember
a few years back,

18:34.760 --> 18:36.399
people used to
make all those jokes

18:36.468 --> 18:37.905
about how Ryan
Seacrest was gay?

18:37.973 --> 18:39.913
And then he started making
those jokes himself,

18:39.981 --> 18:41.485
and now nobody makes
those jokes anymore.

18:41.554 --> 18:42.791
I mean, he's still gay,

18:42.859 --> 18:45.033
but now it's no fun
to joke about it,

18:45.101 --> 18:46.907
because he-he beat
us to the punch.

18:46.975 --> 18:48.714
My God!

18:48.782 --> 18:52.093
That little pole-smoker's
a (bleep) genius!

18:54.369 --> 18:56.745
...and so did the Corinthians
finally write back

18:56.813 --> 18:58.852
to Saint Paul, saying,

18:58.920 --> 19:00.626
"Dude, enough with the letters.

19:00.693 --> 19:01.964
"We have received them all,

19:02.033 --> 19:04.540
"and will get back to you
when we have the time.

19:04.609 --> 19:05.912
"And by the way,

19:05.980 --> 19:07.719
"a lot of the information
you're asking for

19:07.787 --> 19:08.790
is available online."

19:10.933 --> 19:13.710
Oh, look, everybody,
it's the burning bush.

19:13.777 --> 19:15.616
(crowd murmuring)

19:19.432 --> 19:21.237
Hello, Father.

19:21.306 --> 19:24.416
I thought I made it clear that
you are no longer welcome here.

19:24.484 --> 19:27.227
You know, I've been coming
to this church for years.

19:27.295 --> 19:29.000
I've heard all the stories.

19:29.068 --> 19:30.639
Who did Jesus hang around with?

19:30.708 --> 19:32.079
Mary Magdalene.

19:32.147 --> 19:33.350
And who was she?

19:33.418 --> 19:34.655
A prostitute.

19:34.723 --> 19:35.827
Which means,

19:35.895 --> 19:37.767
if they had cameras back then,

19:37.835 --> 19:39.708
<i>I bet she would have done
a porno.</i>

19:39.776 --> 19:42.017
(crowd murmuring)

19:42.990 --> 19:45.230
(whirring)

19:45.281 --> 19:47.037
And if she did,

19:47.104 --> 19:49.513
I know that Jesus
would have forgiven her.

19:49.581 --> 19:52.357
Am I any worse
than Mary Magdalene?

19:52.425 --> 19:56.239
And more importantly,
are you all better than Jesus?

19:56.307 --> 19:57.979
I'm better
than Jesus.

19:58.047 --> 20:00.690
Okay, yes, Tina Fey,
you're better than Jesus.

20:00.756 --> 20:02.362
But the rest of you...

20:02.431 --> 20:04.637
The rest of you need
to accept the fact

20:04.706 --> 20:06.880
that I made a simple mistake.

20:06.947 --> 20:08.285
And here it is.

20:10.996 --> 20:12.768
(projector clicking,
music playing)

20:39.438 --> 20:40.508
(all gasping)

20:53.559 --> 20:58.142
I know I'm a man of God...
but that (bleep) is hot!

20:58.211 --> 20:59.932
(applause, cheering
and whooping)

21:09.520 --> 21:10.991
Oh, look at that.

21:11.059 --> 21:12.932
See, now I'm really starting
to get suspicious.

21:13.000 --> 21:15.107
Somebody order a pizza?

21:15.108 --> 22:16.108
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru